codex
Both probes together give the real semantics: ungrouped vertices survive longest; within the group, higher weight collapses earlier. So "protection" means *leaving features out of the group*, and priority ordering comes from graduated victim weights. This also reveals v1's `vertex_group_factor=1000` path was inverted (it never executed, so no harm in the published full bundle).

Now I'll write the v2 script: whole-mesh seam-free reduction (dissolve + one priority-weighted collapse), a real fidelity suite (exact plane-section polylines with symmetric Hausdorff, tooth count/clock at y=6, +X floor radius every 0.1 mm on the ramp, silhouette bounds), a deterministic profile ladder, the 15k/20k/25k/30k budget curve on lite failure, geometry hashes for rerun determinism, and all evidence writes under `-v2` names.
