codex
This explains everything: the ramp region (9.6–14.1 mm) holds 113,937 of 139,886 triangles — the hob's runout scallops — while the tooth band is only 13.5k. The ramp is the collapse pool, not the thing to protect; its scallop amplitude is what the 0.05 mm bound tolerates (v1's accidental ramp collapse measured 0.017 max). And to reach 14.5k, the prismatic tooth band must also merge axial rings, so it needs a small weight rather than zero. Rewriting the ladder around the real geometry:
