codex
The error is one-directional and localized: source→candidate 0.0968 mm in the tooth region only (everywhere else ≤ 0.008; candidate→source ≤ 0.006). The collapse removed a source feature between section planes — likely at the tooth-end runout exit, not the flank profile. The lite run is still going; its numbers plus the failure curve will tell me whether lite can meet 0.05 mm at all. Polling:
