codex
The dissolve curve per region is decisive: the tooth band dissolves to 7.1k at 0.005 rad and 5.3k at 0.01 rad — position-preserving, so section profiles stay intact — while the ramp dissolves to 70.9k/45.9k and above20 barely dissolves at all (real curvature, so it needs collapse). A feasible lite budget: dissolve 0.01 (tooth 5,291 + journal 872 + below3 299) + above20 collapsed to ~3,500 + ramp to ~4,500 ≈ 14.5k, with the tooth band never in a collapse pool.

This calls for a regional reducer: dissolve, then group-targeted collapse passes on ramp/above20 only, with the tooth band and silhouette-guarded extremes excluded from every pool. Stopping the old run (its failure mode is now explained) and rewriting:
