codex
Lite attempt 1 fails on sections (0.128 mm) even with the tooth band untouched — so the 0.12 mm error was never tooth collapse; it's the ramp scallops themselves at the 10.92/12/13.78 planes. The hob scallop amplitude (~0.12 mm) exceeds the 0.05 mm criterion once the ramp is compressed to ~4.5k triangles, while the floor-radius trend stays accurate (0.005 mm). This is exactly the infeasibility case the spec anticipates. Letting the ladder, export, and failure curve complete:
diff --git a/scripts/manufacturing/export_study.py b/scripts/manufacturing/export_study.py
